    hook: "Giraffes did not choose to have long necks. Cheetahs did not decide to be fast. These traits evolved over millions of years through natural selection — the process by which organisms with traits better suited to their environment survive and reproduce more than others. Over countless generations, helpful traits become more common and species change. Evolution is the unifying theory of biology — it explains the diversity of life, the similarities between species, and the history of life on Earth. Cosmo the Otter is the product of millions of years of evolution that shaped every feature of his body.",
