    hook: "Your body maintains a temperature of 98.6°F whether you are in a snowstorm or a desert. Your blood sugar stays stable whether you just ate or have not eaten for hours. This remarkable stability is called homeostasis — your body's ability to maintain a constant internal environment despite changing external conditions. Eleven major body systems work together every second to keep you alive and balanced. Cosmo the Otter maintains his body temperature in freezing water — homeostasis at work.",
